<span class="eyebrow">Services</span>
<h1>Full-home renovation design in Toronto</h1>
<p>A full-home renovation changes how a house works: new layouts, opened or moved walls, new kitchens and bathrooms, and finishes throughout. Renotect designs the whole project, prepares the permit drawings in-house and follows the work on site, so you deal with one studio from the first sketch to the final walkthrough.</p>
<div class="cta" style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href="/#contact">Book a free consultation</a><a class="btn alt" href="tel:+14372549794">Call (437) 254-9794</a></div>
</div></section>

<figure class="imgband"><img src="/images/projects/north-york-custom-home-1.jpg" alt="Custom home facade in North York designed by Renotect" width="1600" height="900" decoding="async"><figcaption class="wrap">North York custom home</figcaption></figure>

<section><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">What is included</span>
<h2>One studio for design, drawings and site</h2></div>
<p class="lead">Every renovation is scoped around your house, budget and schedule. These are the parts we take care of.</p></div>
<ol class="svc">
<li><span class="n">01</span><h3>Existing conditions</h3><p>We measure and document the house as it is today, so the design starts from accurate drawings.</p></li>
<li><span class="n">02</span><h3>Layout and space planning</h3><p>New layouts for how you want to live: open plans, better flow, more storage and light.</p></li>
<li><span class="n">03</span><h3>3D visuals and material boards</h3><p>You see the rooms, finishes and lighting before anything is ordered or demolished.</p></li>
<li><span class="n">04</span><h3>Structural changes</h3><p>Moving or removing walls and openings, coordinated with a structural engineer where the design needs one.</p></li>
<li><span class="n">05</span><h3>Permit and construction drawings</h3><p>A BCIN-qualified designer prepares the drawings for permit and for contractors to price the same, clearly defined job.</p></li>
<li><span class="n">06</span><h3>Site oversight</h3><p>The person who designed your home follows it on site through construction, so the build matches the design.</p></li>
</ol>
</div></section>

<section style="background:var(--card);border-block:1px solid var(--line)"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head"><div><span class="eyebrow">Permits</span>
<h2>Does your renovation need a permit?</h2></div></div>
<div class="about" style="margin-top:28px">
<p>In Toronto and the rest of Ontario, work that changes the structure of a house, adds space, moves or adds plumbing, or changes how a space is used usually needs a building permit from the municipality. Cosmetic work such as painting, new flooring or replacing cabinets in the same layout usually does not.</p>
<p>We tell you early which approvals your project needs, and prepare the drawings for them as part of the design. Read more about our <a href="/services/permit-drawings-toronto/">permit drawings for houses and small buildings</a>.</p>
</div>
</div></section>

